# Wishlist Patterns

## Always Use `useWishlist()` — Never Access Store Directly

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD
const { has, toggle, ids, isAuthenticated } = useWishlist();

// ❌ BAD — bypasses auth check and userId scoping
const ids = useWishlistStore((s) => s.map['some-id']);
```

## Auth Gate

`toggle()` from `useWishlist()` automatically redirects to `/login` if the user is not authenticated. No extra auth check needed in components.

```typescript
<button onClick={() => toggle(item.id)}>♥</button>
// → if not logged in: router.push('/login')
// → if logged in: toggles wishlist for current user
```

## Per-User Storage

The wishlist store (`wishlist-store.ts`) uses `map: Record<userId, string[]>`:
- Logged-in users get their own wishlist slot keyed by `user.id`
- Guests use the key `'guest'`
- Logging out preserves the user's wishlist for next login

## Displaying Wishlist Items

Use `useWishlistItems()` to resolve full product data from IDs:

```typescript
const { items, isLoading } = useWishlistItems();
// items: CategoryItem[] — ready for <CategoryProductCard>
```

Used in: `src/modules/profile/components/ProfilePage.tsx` (wishlist tab)

## Wishlist Count

```typescript
const { ids } = useWishlist();
// ids.length = number of items in wishlist for current user
```
